  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset ecosystem in late August 2026 is defined by high-stakes regulatory milestones and architectural competition at the protocol layer. The impending September 15 U.S. Senate cloture vote on the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633) serves as the primary macro catalyst, creating intense market focus around regulatory definitions. Simultaneously, institutional Bitcoin adoption matures past initial speculative ETF inflows into deeper corporate treasury integration and multi-asset portfolio balancing, while cross-chain architecture moves away from vulnerable wrapped tokens toward non-custodial direct swaps. Technologically, institutional preference for deterministic execution environments like Clarity on Bitcoin-native layers is challenging traditional EVM dominance by mitigating complex smart contract vulnerabilities.",
